2.1 Experiment 1: Student Grades Case Study in SIAKAD — FOR Loop
A lecturer enters the quiz scores of 10 students and the program determines the highest and lowest scores.
The program also counts the number of students who pass and fail. A passing score is 60 or higher. 
Based on this case, build the Java program using the steps below.

2.1.1 Java Program Code
import java.util.Scanner;

public class SiakadFor264107020237 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        double score, highest = Double.NEGATIVE_INFINITY;
        double lowest = Double.POSITIVE_INFINITY;

        for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
            System.out.print("Enter score for student " + i + ": ");
            score = sc.nextDouble();

            if (score > highest) {
                highest = score;
            }
            if (score < lowest) {
                lowest = score;
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Highest score: " + highest);
        System.out.println("Lowest score : " + lowest);
        sc.close();
    }
}

